%S A398909 1,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,3,0,10,12,35,52,19,20,349,360,636,3667,15180,11844,
%T A398909 13286,10939,27173,36990,200944,509090,1991612,4857123,11233243,
%U A398909 35636235,62913698,129632856,257789382,189997570,685074253,2192533549,5107290522,9128866565,19743697660,44622335651
%N A398909 Number of essentially different non-circular permutations of the numbers 1 to n such that the sum of adjacent numbers is a square.
%C A398909 The reversals of a permutation are not counted as different.
%C A398909 The first and last numbers of the permutations are required not to have a square sum. Thus this sequence counts the square chains which cannot be closed to form a square loop (circular permutation in A071984).
%C A398909 For comparison, A090460 counts all essentially different square chains, with each square loop counted only once (A071984), and also these non-circular permutations.
%C A398909 For 15 <= n <= 31, there are no square loops, so the terms agree with A090460 and A071983 (Diophante link).
%C A398909 This sequence together with A071983 (essentially different chains with each loop counted n times), A071984 (square loops themselves) and A090460 (essentially different chains with each loop counted only once) gives the four possible distinct counts of square chains.
%C A398909 In graph-theoretic terms, these numbers count Hamiltonian paths whose two endpoints are not adjacent (and hence which cannot be closed to form a Hamiltonian cycle), with reversals not counted as distinct.
%H A398909 Diophante, <a href="http://www.diophante.fr/problemes-par-themes/h-graphes-et-circuits/696-h119-les-colliers-de-perles">H178 = H119. Les colliers de perles (ouverts et fermés)</a> (in French).
%F A398909 a(n) = A090460(n) - A071984(n).
%F A398909 a(n) = A071983(n) - n*A071984(n).
%e A398909 a(16) = 1 with this only one possible square chain of length 16 (8, 1, 15, 10, 6, 3, 13, 12, 4, 5, 11, 14, 2, 7, 9, 16) with 16 + 8 = 24 (not square).
%e A398909 a(32) = 360 since there are 360 square chains that are non-circular permutations; another one is the square loop (32, 4, 21, 28, 8, 1, 15, 10, 26, 23, 2, 14, 22, 27, 9, 16, 20, 29, 7, 18, 31, 5, 11, 25, 24, 12, 13, 3, 6, 30, 19, 17), but as 17 + 32 = 49 = 7^2 this square chain is not counted here.
%Y A398909 Cf. A071983 (number of total permutations that counts each circular solution n times), A071984 (number of circular permutations), A090460 (number of total permutations that counts each circular solution only once), this sequence (number of non-circular permutations), A090461.
%K A398909 nonn,hard,new
%O A398909 15,9
